          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کارت به کارت کردن (kârt-be-kârt kardan) — \"to transfer money from card to card\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پول بلیت را برای دوستم کارت به کارت کردم. Pul-e bilit râ barâ-ye dustam kârt-be-kârt kardam. I transferred the ticket money to my friend by card."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Very common in Iran: money goes from one bank card to another by phone or cash machine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "kârt-be-kârt kardan is built from kârt 'card', which EtymDB takes from French carte, twice over with be 'to', and kardan 'to do', inherited from Middle Persian kardan (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
